course: dictionary
lesson: 13957
title: Lighten: less heavy, brighter, happier
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lighten is a word with more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. Then try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have got it.
explain: «Can you lighten my bag? It is too heavy.» Here lighten means make less heavy, because the clue is heavy. «The sky began to lighten as the sun rose.» Here lighten means become brighter, because the clue is the sun rising.
explain: Lighten can also make a feeling or a job easier. «A funny joke lightened the mood in the class.» The mood is the feeling in the room, so lighten means make it happier. «Lighten up!» is informal and means relax and stop being so serious.
fact: Lighten is a verb, so its forms are lighten, lightens, lightened and lightening.
fact: «Lighten» means to make something less heavy, as in «lighten your bag».
fact: «Lighten» means to make or become brighter or paler in colour, as in «the sky lightened».
fact: «Lighten» can mean to make a mood or a job easier or happier, as in «a joke lightened the mood».
fact: «Lighten up» is informal and means relax and stop being so serious.
exercise: «Can you lighten my bag? It is too heavy.» What does lighten mean here? | Make wider | Make louder | Make brighter | *Make less heavy
exercise: «The room began to lighten when the sun came out.» What does lighten mean here? | Stay dark and cold | Become heavier | *Become brighter | Become quieter
exercise: Sam says, «Lighten up, it's only a game!» What does lighten up mean? | Shout more loudly | Paint the walls white | *Relax and stop being so serious | Carry more things
test: «Her kind words lightened the mood after the bad news.» What does lightened the mood mean? | *Made the feeling happier and easier | Made the mood louder | Made the mood sadder | Made the mood heavier
test: Mum asks, «Can you lighten the box so I can carry it?» Which meaning fits? | Make it louder | Make it brighter | *Make it less heavy | Make it happier
exam: «He added a little white paint to lighten the blue.» Which meaning of lighten fits best here? | *To make the blue paler | To make the blue heavier | To make the blue sadder | To make the room louder
